WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.340
Imagine a sheet of paper, nought
point one millimetres thick.

2
00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.850
Fold it in half.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.730
Now it's twice as thick.

4
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:10.080
Fold again, and again.

5
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:12.150
Every fold doubles it.

6
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.950
How many folds until the
stack reaches the Moon,

7
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.510
on average three hundred
and eighty-four thousand,

8
00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:19.620
four hundred kilometres away?

9
00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:20.950
A thousand folds?

10
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.360
Over a million?

11
00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.900
In this mission, you'll treat
doubling as an exponential:

12
00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:30.650
two to the five is thirty-two,
and two to the n grows fast.

13
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.390
You'll meet logarithms.

14
00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:37.210
A logarithm is a power: it answers
what power of two gives a number.

15
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.440
And you'll see how taking
logs brings the power down,

16
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.240
so you can solve for it.

17
00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:46.840
Your mission: work out how many times
you must fold paper for it to reach the

18
00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:47.490
Moon.
